# Executable scripts + git hooks MUST stay LF.
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite these to CRLF, which
# breaks the `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang (`bash\r`) and trailing-CR token parsing under
# bash. eol=lf here overrides autocrlf so every checkout (macOS/Linux/Windows) gets LF.
# (sos-kit P059 — Windows portability dogfood, 2026-06-09.)
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
hooks/* text eol=lf
bin/*   text eol=lf

# Parity golden fixtures + trust-gate-hashed text families MUST stay LF too.
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true default) rewrites these to CRLF, which:
#   (a) breaks byte-for-byte parity comparisons against `crates/sos-cli/tests/golden/*.golden`
#       (parity_sync_enforced, parity_new_enforced, parity_adopt_enforced)
#   (b) shifts sha256 of `.claude/settings.json` / `.mcp.json` vs the POSIX-seeded
#       trust-gate baseline (P087 BUG 2) — LF-forcing these families closes that
#       CRLF-hash-mismatch structurally.
# Targeted per-glob (kit style, P059 precedent) — NOT `* text=auto` global.
# (sos-kit P088 — Windows checkout/EOL layer, 2026-07-24.)
*.golden text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
